   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>NCLEX practice exam</span></nav><section class="hero w hv"><div><h1>The Full Adaptive NCLEX-RN Practice Exam</h1><p class="lead">A full computerized adaptive test that gets harder or easier as you answer, then stops by the same rules as the NCLEX. Finish with a pass likelihood, category scores, and a study plan.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#start/exam">Start the exam</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#start/quick">Quick round of 30</a></div></div><figure class="shot duo"><div class="duo-s"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-q-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-q-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-q-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 72px), 560px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam in progress: item 5 with the five-hour timer, calculator and an answer selected" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div></div><div class="dv dv-p dv-po" style="--sb:#1c497e"><div class="dv-s"><div class="dv-sb lt" aria-hidden="true"><time class="vx-now" data-f="sb"></time><span class="dv-isl"></span><span class="dv-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 18 12" width="17" height="11"><rect x="0" y="8" width="3" height="4" rx=".8"/><rect x="5" y="5.5" width="3" height="6.5" rx=".8"/><rect x="10" y="3" width="3" height="9" rx=".8"/><rect x="15" y="0" width="3" height="12" rx=".8"/></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 16 12" width="15" height="11"><path d="M8 11.6 5.6 9.2a3.4 3.4 0 0 1 4.8 0z"/><path d="M3.4 7A6.5 6.5 0 0 1 12.6 7l-1.3 1.3a4.7 4.7 0 0 0-6.6 0z"/><path d="M1.1 4.7a9.7 9.7 0 0 1 13.8 0l-1.3 1.3a7.9 7.9 0 0 0-11.2 0z"/></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 27 13" width="25" height="12"><rect x=".6" y=".6" width="22.8" height="11.8" rx="3.4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".4" stroke-width="1.2"/><rect x="2.4" y="2.4" width="17.6" height="8.2" rx="2"/><path d="M25 4.4v4.2c.9-.3 1.4-1.1 1.4-2.1s-.5-1.8-1.4-2.1z" fill-opacity=".45"/></svg></span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-phone-780.webp" srcset="/img/exam-phone-400.webp 400w, /img/exam-phone-780.webp 780w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 30vw, 160px" width="780" height="1600" alt="The full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam on a phone, with the timer and an answer selected" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div></div></div><figcaption>The full exam in progress, on a laptop and a phone. Demo student.</figcaption></figure></section><div class="w"><h2>Built like the real exam</h2><div class="feat"><div><b>Adaptive</b>Each answer changes the difficulty of the next question.</div><div><b>85 to 150 items</b>Including unscored pretest items, just like test day.</div><div><b>5-hour clock</b>With optional breaks.</div><div><b>Real stopping rules</b>95% confidence, maximum length, or out of time.</div><div><b>NGN case studies</b>Unfolding cases with partial-credit scoring.</div><div><b>Test-day mode</b>Optional full screen, timing, and integrity checks for realistic practice.</div></div>
     <div class="split"><div class="st"><h2>NGN case studies, inside the exam</h2><p>Unfolding case studies put the patient's history, notes and vital signs beside the question, and select-all and matrix items earn partial credit, the way they do on the real NCLEX.</p></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-ngn-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-ngn-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-ngn-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="A Next Generation NCLEX case study inside the full practice exam, with the patient history tabs beside a highlight item" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>An NGN case study inside the full exam. Fictional patient.</figcaption></figure></div>
     <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-results-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-results-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-results-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Full practice exam results for a demo student: a 74% pass-likelihood estimate, labeled as an estimate, with ability by item" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>End-of-exam results for a demo student: a pass-likelihood estimate (an estimate, not a prediction) and ability by item.</figcaption></figure>
     <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-results-cats-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-results-cats-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-results-cats-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Full practice exam results by NCLEX client needs category, from below to above the passing standard" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Every client needs category, from below to above the passing standard.</figcaption></figure>
     <h2>What you get at the end</h2><ul><li>A pass likelihood based on your ability estimate.</li><li>Scores for each of the 8 client needs categories.</li><li>A study plan built from your weakest areas.</li><li>Rationales and sources for every item.</li></ul>
     <h2>How to use it</h2><p>Take one full exam early to find your baseline, study your weakest categories with topic drills, then retest every week or two. A quick round of 30 questions works well on busy days.</p><h2>Rehearse test day before test day</h2><p>In the last two weeks before your NCLEX, take at least one full exam in test-day mode: a locked screen, webcam checks, a clock that keeps running on breaks, and an integrity report at the end. <a href="/nclex-test-day-simulation">See how the test-day simulation works</a>.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#start/testday">Start a proctored practice exam</a></div><p>Proctored full exams with 85+ questions that end in a Pass with a Clean integrity report count toward the <a href="/nclex-pass-guarantee">NCLEX pass guarantee, a registration-fee reimbursement for students who qualify and don't pass</a>.</p>
     <style>
.vx-val{margin:34px 0}.vx-val h2{margin-top:0}
.vx-cmp{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,230px),1fr));gap:12px;margin:16px 0}
.vx-cmp>div{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;display:grid;gap:4px;align-content:start}
.vx-cmp b{font:400 20px/1.2 var(--fh)}.vx-cmp .amt{font:700 24px/1.2 var(--fb);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink)}.vx-cmp small{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;line-height:1.4}
.vx-cmp .vx-us{background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy);color:var(--navy-ink)}.vx-cmp .vx-us .amt,.vx-cmp .vx-us b{color:var(--navy-ink)}.vx-cmp .vx-us small{color:var(--navy-ink);opacity:.85}
.vx-calc{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:4px solid var(--gold);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:18px 0}
.vx-calc h3{margin:0 0 8px}.vx-calc .vc-in{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 16px;align-items:center}.vx-calc label{font-weight:700}
.vx-calc input[type=range]{flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0;accent-color:var(--accent)}.vx-calc input[type=number]{width:96px;font:17px var(--fb);padding:7px 9px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink)}
.vx-calc fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:10px 0 0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 18px}.vx-calc legend{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:4px;padding:0}.vx-calc fieldset label{font-weight:400;display:inline-flex;gap:6px;align-items:center}
.vx-out{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,200px),1fr));gap:10px;margin:14px 0 4px}.vx-out>div{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px}
.vx-out span{display:block;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.vx-out output{display:block;font:700 22px/1.25 var(--fb);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.vx-out small{color:var(--muted)}
.vx-note{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:6px 0 0}
.vx-ps{max-width:520px}.vx-ps td:nth-child(n+3),.vx-ps th:nth-child(n+3){text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
.vx-scale{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(100%,220px),1fr));gap:8px 18px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:12px 0}.vx-scale li{line-height:1.35}.vx-scale b{color:var(--accent)}
.vx-fn{font-size:14px}.vx-fn td,.vx-fn th{padding:6px 8px}.vx-fn a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.vx-strip{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--gold);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:30px 0}
.vx-strip h2{font-size:clamp(22px,3.2vw,28px);margin:0 0 6px}.vx-strip ul{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:10px 0}
.vx-strip li{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:14.5px}.vx-strip li b{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.vx-strip p{margin:6px 0}</style><aside class="vx-strip" aria-labelledby="vxs-h"><h2 id="vxs-h">One license instead of separate tools</h2><p>One license covers what schools usually buy as separate tools, and it's free for every student and instructor.</p><ul><li>Academic EHR seat: <b>about $110–$145</b></li><li>Clinical day and attendance tracking: <b>about $35–$140</b></li><li>Supplemental NCLEX review layer: <b>about $229–$389</b></li><li>Vexcura, everything: <b>$50–$99</b> per student</li></ul><p class="vx-note">Typical published prices per student per year, as of November 2026; your costs may differ. Vexcura doesn't replace proctored assessments. <a href="/for-nursing-schools#value">Compare costs and see the sources</a></p></aside><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><h3>How do I get access to the practice exam?</h3><p>Through your nursing program. Vexcura is licensed to nursing schools and facilities, so students and instructors never pay: join with the code from your instructor. If your program doesn't use Vexcura yet, send your faculty to nclexsim.com/for-nursing-schools. The public practice questions and study guides on this site are free for everyone.</p><h3>Is the practice exam free?</h3><p>Yes for students: the school or facility pays for the license, and there are no student plans. The free practice questions and study guides on this site need no account at all.</p><h3>How many questions are on the practice exam?</h3><p>Between 85 and 150, the same range as the NCLEX-RN, including unscored pretest items and unfolding case studies. You have up to 5 hours.</p><h3>How does the practice exam decide when to stop?</h3><p>It uses the same three stopping rules as the NCLEX: it ends when it is 95% confident your ability is above or below the passing standard, when you reach 150 items, or when the 5 hours run out.</p><h3>Is the pass likelihood accurate?</h3><p>It is an estimate from your answers in this question bank. The bank's difficulty ratings are not calibrated by NCSBN, so treat it as a guide to your readiness, not a prediction of your result.</p><h3>Can I take it on my phone?</h3><p>Yes. The exam works in any modern browser on a phone, tablet, or computer. For test-day mode, use a laptop or desktop like the one at the testing center.</p><h3>How many practice exams can I take?</h3><p>As many as you like. Your results, category scores, and study plan update after each exam.</p></div>
     <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Pass likelihood is an estimate from this question bank, whose difficulty ratings are not calibrated by NCSBN. It does not predict or guarantee your NCLEX result.</p><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/nclex-test-day-simulation">Proctored test-day rehearsal</a></li><li><a href="/next-generation-nclex">Next Generation NCLEX (NGN) guide</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-pass-guarantee">NCLEX pass guarantee: registration fee back if you qualify and don't pass</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-practice-questions">Free NCLEX practice questions by category</a></li><li><a href="/ati-score-report-study-plan">Turn your ATI score report into a study plan</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-study-guides">Free NCLEX study guides (PDF)</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-prep-comparison">NCLEX prep compared</a></li><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Bring Vexcura to your nursing program</h2><p>1,220 cited NCLEX-RN questions, adaptive practice exams, 8 NGN case studies, an Epic-style academic EHR and a clinical instructor workspace. The school pays; students and instructors are always free, and every plan includes everything. Students: ask your instructor, or join with your school's code.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools">See Vexcura for nursing schools</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#signup">Join with a school code</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot"><div class="w"><div class="cols">
   <div><p class="fh">Vexcura</p><p>NCLEX-RN prep and an Epic-style academic EHR, licensed to nursing schools and facilities. Free for students and instructors. Built by a registered nurse.</p></div>
